---
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
---
<SiteLayout
  title="Independent operating system development"
  description="December Reach is an independent operating system development organization. Explore its OS projects, platform architecture and web emulation model."
  current="home"
>
  <section class="panorama-intro" aria-labelledby="home-title">
    <div class="identity">
      <p class="identity-description">Independent operating system development</p>
      <h1 id="home-title">December<br />Reach</h1>
    </div>
    <div class="intro-detail">
      <p class="intro-statement">Operating systems,<br />built to be reached.</p>
      <p class="intro-copy">
        December Reach develops operating systems and the technology that makes
        their real source accessible through the web. The site acquires and
        preloads source; emulation runs in a separate JavaScript backend.
      </p>
      <a class="metro-link" href="https://github.com/DecemberReach/reach-to-be-reached" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
        Explore the OS source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panorama-section systems-section" id="systems" aria-labelledby="systems-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <h2 id="systems-title">Operating systems</h2>
      <p>Different environments. Separate system identities.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="system-panorama">
      <article class="system-tile tile-aurora">
        <span class="tile-number">01</span>
        <div class="tile-content">
          <h3>auroraADE</h3>
          <p>Aesthetic Desktop Environment. Its documented target architecture is x86_64.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="tile-context">Desktop environment</span>
      </article>
      <article class="system-tile tile-halo">
        <span class="tile-number">02</span>
        <div class="tile-content">
          <h3>haloDOT</h3>
          <p>An operating-system project in the December Reach lineup.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="tile-context">OS project</span>
      </article>
      <article class="system-tile tile-stella">
        <span class="tile-number">03</span>
        <div class="tile-content">
          <h3>stellaOS</h3>
          <p>A television operating system in the reachOS lineup.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="tile-context">TV operating system</span>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="panorama-section platform-section" id="platform" aria-labelledby="platform-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <h2 id="platform-title">Platform architecture</h2>
      <p>
        Fabric Dessert defines the virtual board and hardware-facing contracts
        used by the reachOS platform. It remains separate from the browser host.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="specification-list">
      <div class="specification-row">
        <span class="specification-name">CPU boundary</span>
        <strong>FRT64</strong>
        <p>Integration boundary for ARM and x86, 32-bit and 64-bit.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="specification-row">
        <span class="specification-name">Physical memory</span>
        <strong>64-bit address space</strong>
        <p>BigInt-backed addressing with sparse memory regions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="specification-row">
        <span class="specification-name">Device bus</span>
        <strong>MMIO / IRQ</strong>
        <p>Device windows, alignment, interrupt lines and enumeration.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="specification-row">
        <span class="specification-name">Display</span>
        <strong>1080 × 2424</strong>
        <p>RGBA8888 framebuffer with a deterministic host-canvas bridge.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <a class="metro-link section-link" href="/architecture/">Read the platform architecture <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="panorama-section execution-section" id="web-access" aria-labelledby="execution-title">
    <header class="section-heading">
      <h2 id="execution-title">The web is the way in.<br />Not the machine.</h2>
      <p>
        Source preparation, system execution and web access are separate
        responsibilities. The browser is not the guest machine's execution host.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="execution-sequence">
      <article class="execution-step">
        <span class="step-number">01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Source acquisition</h3>
          <p>The frontend obtains and preloads the real operating-system source.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="execution-step">
        <span class="step-number">02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>JavaScript backend</h3>
          <p>The backend owns emulation and the system execution environment.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="execution-step">
        <span class="step-number">03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Web access</h3>
          <p>The browser provides access to the running system session.</p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a class="metro-link section-link" href="/emulation/">Understand the emulation model <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </section>

  <section class="closing-line" aria-label="December Reach source">
    <p>The source is the work.</p>
    <a class="metro-link" href="https://github.com/DecemberReach/reach-to-be-reached" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">
      Open reach-to-be-reached <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
    </a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
